Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 45\u00b0F was the 20th coolest November 13 high of 105 since 1922, the coolest since 2019.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 82% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>45\u00b0F</strong> was the 20th coolest November 13 high of 105 since 1922, the coolest since 2019. The normal high for the date is 53\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1964). The low of <strong>37\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Allentown's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Allentown has set <strong>55 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 94 that chance alone would give, and <strong>100 record highs</strong>, close to the 95 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (46). Allentown's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on July 3, 1966.","t_chg":"Allentown has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 98 complete years: Allentown's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.19\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.27), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1925. Allentown's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.28), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1925.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Allentown's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.32 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 47.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (71.72 in); the driest, 1980 (29.82 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}